WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
1987.

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:06.310
States sign the Montreal Protocol, to
phase out chemicals that destroy the ozone

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.370
layer.

4
00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:12.910
The ozone layer is now projected to
recover around 2066 over the Antarctic.

5
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.550
But the atmosphere is not the
only thing that crosses borders.

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.830
So do the high seas, migrating
wildlife and shared rivers.

7
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.090
No country can fix them alone.

8
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.250
So why do so many other
global agreements struggle?

9
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.490
Too little money?

10
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.770
Disputed science?

11
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.430
In this mission, you'll follow one treaty
from signing to the ozone layer's projected

12
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.670
recovery.

13
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.810
Then you'll test other
agreements against it,

14
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.550
on wildlife trade, ocean
zones and the Nile.

15
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.830
Your mission: judge what makes a
global environmental agreement succeed.
